{"id": "185835", "name": "01-x^3=y^3", "qtype": "truefalse", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 1, "options": {}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\">\n<div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ W = \\{(x,y,z) : x^3 = y^3 \\} \\]</p>\n<p>Is <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(W\\)</span> a subspace of <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(\\mathbb{R}^3\\)</span>?</p>\n</div>\n</div><div class=\"native-answer\">[[input:ans]]</div>", "generalfeedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:12px 16px;margin-bottom:12px\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Outline:</b> We check the three conditions: the zero vector, closure under addition, closure under scalar multiplication.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 1 — Simplify the condition</b><br>Over <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(\\mathbb{R}\\)</span> the function <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(t\\mapsto t^3\\)</span> is strictly increasing, hence one-to-one: <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(x^3=y^3\\)</span> holds exactly when <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(x=y\\)</span>. So<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ W=\\{(x,y,z): x=y\\}=\\{(x,y,z): x-y=0\\}. \\]</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 2 — The three conditions</b><br><span dir=\"ltr\">\\((0,0,0)\\)</span> satisfies <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(0-0=0\\)</span>. If <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(x_1=y_1\\)</span> and <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(x_2=y_2\\)</span>, then <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(x_1+x_2=y_1+y_2\\)</span> and <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(\\lambda x_1=\\lambda y_1\\)</span> for every <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(\\lambda\\in\\mathbb{R}\\)</span>. So <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(W\\)</span> contains zero and is closed under addition and scalar multiplication (it is the solution set of a homogeneous linear equation, a plane through the origin).\n<p style=\"text-align:center\"><b>The statement is true.</b></p></div></div>", "specificfeedback": "[[feedback:prt1]]", "prtcorrect": "", "prtpartiallycorrect": "", "prtincorrect": "", "inputs": [{"name": "ans", "type": "radio", "boxsize": 15, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": false, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": false, "showvalidation": 0, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": "", "native": {"shuffle": false, "numbering": "none", "instruction": "one", "lang": "en"}}], "prts": [{"name": "prt1", "value": 1, "native": true, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": []}], "qvnames": [], "nvariants": 1}